      "message": "NIT:\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts disables lifecycle scripts for install, but the subsequent npm audit step runs without --ignore-scripts. npm audit itself does not execute install scripts, but tooling drift is worth guarding against.\n\nWhy: Defense-in-depth — the stated security posture is \"lifecycle scripts disabled\". Making that explicit at every npm invocation prevents future refactors from silently re-enabling script execution.\n\nRecommendation: No change strictly required, but consider setting NPM_CONFIG_IGNORE_SCRIPTS: true at the job env: level so any future npm invocation inherits the safe default:\n\n```\njobs:\n    audit:\n        ...\n        env:\n            NPM_CONFIG_IGNORE_SCRIPTS: \u0027true\u0027\n```",
